    "stance": "regular",
    "bio": "Caitlin 'Caity' Simmers is the 2024 WSL Women's World Champion and the youngest women's world champion in history, claiming the title at just 18 years old. Born in Oceanside, California on October 26, 2005, she began surfing at a young age and first won the 2021 US Open of Surfing at age 15 — the second-youngest champion in the event's history. At just 15 she qualified for the WSL Championship Tour but famously turned it down to stay close to family and develop her surfing further. She re-qualified in 2022 and debuted on the CT in 2023, immediately winning 2 CT events and finishing 5th overall to claim the WSL Rookie of the Year award. In 2024 she dominated the regular season, won the WSL Finals over defending champion Caroline Marks 2-1, and cemented her place as the world's best. She competed at the 2024 Paris Olympics (Teahupo'o), finishing 9th. Known for combining explosive competitive surfing with a relaxed freesurfer style, she also skateboards, dances hip hop, and edits her own surf films.",
