    "fax": "(386) 426-0955",
    "surfReport": "24-hour surf report line: (904) 423-2317",
    "bio": "NSB's anchor surf shop and the heartbeat of East Coast surfing for over two decades. Charlie Baldwin and Jennifer Payseur started it in 1980 as a beachside hotdog wagon — literally selling hotdogs from a wagon on Flagler Ave while also running surf contests on top of the wagon. It grew into a full surf shop at 510 Flagler Ave, stocking CB Surfboards and acting as the region's primary sponsor of local competitions. The shop ran a 24-hour surf report line at (904) 423-2317. Bobbie Ewers Werner served as shop manager, overseeing the Swim Wear & Beach Fashions section and buying Surf and Sports Wear. Inlet Charley's hosted Gotcha team autograph signings with Rob Machado, Chris Ward, and Brock Little in 1995 and 1997 — confirmed by Bobbie Ewers Werner in a December 2025 Facebook post. Charlie Baldwin sold Inlet Charley's in 2004; Rip Curl took over the lease on the 510 Flagler Ave location — Rip Curl was confirmed still operating the Flagler Ave location as of December 2025 (per Bobbie Werner's post). The legacy lives on through CB Surfboards.",
