    "hometown": "Bordeaux, France",
    "bio": "Justine Dupont (born August 27, 1991 in Bordeaux) is a French professional surfer and the most decorated female big-wave surfer in history. She began surfing at 11 and was French national longboard champion at 15. She holds the record for the second-largest measured wave ever surfed by a woman — 70.5 ft (21.5 m) at Nazaré in February 2020 (behind Maya Gabeira's 73.5 ft on the same day). A 12-time XXL World Champion, 3-time Nazaré Tow Challenge champion, and 2019 ISA Stand Up Paddle World Champion, she was the first woman to surf the 15m Belharra in France in 2013. In 2023 she was among the first women ever invited to compete in The Eddie Aikau Invitational and surfed a potential world-record wave at Cortes Bank, 110 miles off the California coast. In 2025 she won the Nazaré Big Wave Challenge and placed second among the men. She has starred in HBO's '100 Foot Wave' since 2022. A Heavy Water Surf member and key figure in Surfline's Twenty Foot Plus platform.",
