    "bio": "Laura Enever is a New South Wales professional who competed on the Women's Championship Tour and later became a big-wave surfing pioneer. In January 2023 she set the Guinness World Record for the largest wave ever paddled into by a woman, catching a massive wave at Jaws (Pe'ahi) on Maui estimated at over 40 feet. Her transition from CT competitor to big-wave icon represents one of the most remarkable career evolutions in women's surfing history.",
