    "bio": "Matt Rode is a surfer, writer, and explorer who has spent over a decade as a staff contributor for Surfline and Magicseaweed. Known for obsessively seeking out uncharted and little-known surf breaks worldwide, he has spent years systematically studying swell patterns, coastlines, and bathymetry to find and document new spots. He leads Surfline's flagship travel series 'Maps to Nowhere,' produced in partnership with O'Neill, which sends professional surfers like Ian Crane, Brett Barley, Soli Bailey, Caity Simmers, and Jordy Smith to remote and rarely surfed destinations for feature-length film documentation. He also works for Hawaiian South Shore on Maui. He has surfed Mavericks and other big-wave venues and is planning surf and adventure retreats in Japan with his partner.",
