    "era": "2000s-present",
    "bio": "Snapper Rocks is a right-hand point break at Coolangatta on the southern Gold Coast of Queensland, Australia, which becomes the start of the Superbank — an artificially extended sand formation created by the Tweed River sand bypass that runs through Snapper, Greenmount, and Kirra for up to two kilometers of continuous wave. The Superbank produces some of the longest rides in the world and hosted the Quiksilver Pro Gold Coast as the traditional CT season opener for many years.",
