    "hometown": "Byron Bay, New South Wales, Australia",
    "stance": "regular",
    "bio": "Soli Bailey is an Australian professional surfer from Byron Bay, NSW, and the first pro surfer to compete under the Australian Aboriginal flag at the top level of surfing. He began surfing at age two in Byron Bay and was winning contests by his mid-teens. He won the ASP Australasia Pro Junior Series in 2014 and qualified for the WSL Championship Tour in 2018. Known as one of the most well-rounded surfers in the world, he excels in everything from technical air reverses to heavy slabs and big waves — Cloudbreak, Shipsterns Bluff, and outer reef bombs. He appeared in multiple seasons of Surfline's Maps to Nowhere series and in his own freesurfing film 'Conehead.' He is an O'Neill team rider and a vocal advocate for Indigenous Australian culture and ocean conservation.",
