    "bio": "Uluwatu is a famous left-hand reef break on the tip of the Bukit Peninsula in Bali, Indonesia. Discovered by western surfers in the early 1970s and featured in Alby Falzon's iconic film Morning of the Earth (1972), Uluwatu became a defining discovery of the surf exploration era. The wave peels along a cliff-lined reef with multiple sections — The Racetrack, Temples, Bombie — and is one of the most consistent and surfed waves in Asia, now surrounded by a thriving surf tourism industry.",
